      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`--schedule-policy routing-key` moves waiting requests whose routing key is in the running batch to the front. The remaining requests should keep their arrival order, but `_sort_by_routing_key` sorts them by `(1, 0, key or \"\")`, which orders them by the key string. A request with key `\"zebra\"` is overtaken by every later request with key `\"apple\"`, and key-less requests overtake both. Whether a request waits then depends on how its key sorts alphabetically, not on when it arrived.\n\nExample: the running batch holds keys `hot`, `hot` and `warm`, and the queue in arrival order is `zebra`, `apple`, `warm`, (no key), `hot`.\n\n- `main`: `hot, warm, no-key, apple, zebra`\n- this PR: `hot, warm, zebra, apple, no-key`\n\n## Modifications\n\n- The sort key for requests outside the running keys is now a constant, so the stable sort keeps their arrival order. The requests whose key is running are ordered as before: by count, then by key, so requests with the same key stay together.\n- New test `TestRoutingKeyPolicy.test_requests_outside_the_running_keys_keep_arrival_order` in `test/registered/unit/managers/test_schedule_policy.py`. It fails on `main` with the order shown above.\n\nNot changed here: like before, this policy ignores `--enable-priority-scheduling`, whereas `fcfs` and `lof` order by priority. I left that alone because it is a policy decision.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable. No model-side change.\n\n## Benchmarking and Profiling\n\nNot applicable. The sort key is only smaller.\n\nHow I tested: CPU only. On `main` (efc9849520) the new test fails and the other 11 tests in the file pass. With this change all 12 pass.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit). I ran isort 7.0.0, ruff 0.15.1 (format, plus the pre-commit `--select=F401,F821,F823,UP037` check) and codespell 2.4.1 on the changed files.\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). Not needed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40102240012](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40102240012)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40102240086](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40102240086)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40102240161](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40102240161)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
